  "answer": "Fixed `normalizeText` in `normalize.mjs`.\n\n**Change made:**\n```js\nreturn value.trim().replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').toLowerCase();\n```\n\n**How it satisfies the spec:**\n- `trim()` removes leading/trailing JavaScript whitespace (spaces, tabs, line breaks, etc.).\n- `.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')` collapses every nonempty run of internal whitespace into a single ASCII space. Since trimming happens first, no stray leading/trailing space is introduced.\n- `.toLowerCase()` lowercases all letters via `String.prototype.toLowerCase()`.\n- Empty/whitespace-only input: `trim()` yields `''`, the regex finds no runs, and the result is `''`.\n- Non-string input still throws `TypeError` (guard unchanged).\n\nThe named export `normalizeText` and the public tests were left untouched.",
